Error [jet.ReadOnlyValueNotOwned]: `handle` was not moved here, so it cannot be returned as-is
  --> tests/ui/ownership/lent_union_handle_cannot_outlive_the_call.jet:7:70
    |
  7 | keep: fn(handle: Directory | FileReader) -> Directory | FileReader { handle }
    |                                                                      ^^^^^^
 Why: This function has read access only and does not own the value
 Fix: Return a copy: `return handle.copy()` — or take ownership: `handle: &&Directory | FileReader`. To return borrowed data, declare `-> View<T> from handle` and return a view derived from `handle`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0120

Error [jet.MissingMoveMarker]: `handle` cannot be moved from borrowed storage
  --> tests/ui/ownership/lent_union_handle_cannot_outlive_the_call.jet:9:69
    |
  9 | hold: fn(handle: Directory | FileReader) -> Holder { Holder{handle: handle} }
    |                                                                     ^^^^^^
 Why: `handle` is a read or write parameter, so its caller keeps the value, and `Directory | FileReader` can't be copied into the struct literal
 Fix: Declare the parameter `handle: &&Directory | FileReader` so the caller hands the value over
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

Error [jet.ReadOnlyValueNotOwned]: `handle` was not moved here, so it cannot be captured by a stored lambda
  --> tests/ui/ownership/lent_union_handle_cannot_outlive_the_call.jet:12:5
    |
 12 |     () -> if handle == {
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: This function can access the parameter, but it does not own the value; a capture here takes ownership
 Fix: Make the parameter owned: `handle: &&Directory | FileReader`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0120
